        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add /model aliases for CLI mode commands",
        "summary": "Added aliases `model:<mode>` for all `mode:<mode>` commands in the CLI command registry and slash command data. This allows users to use `/model:<mode>` syntax interchangeably with `/mode:<mode>`. Changes apply to `cli/src/commands/command-registry.ts` and `cli/src/data/slash-commands.ts`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:02:56.797Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You can now type /model:mode instead of /mode:mode to switch the assistant between different modes, and both phrases will work the same way. The system now accepts either word to reach the same command. If you looked, you would see /model:mode treated as an alternate spelling of /mode:mode in the list of available commands. This works today.",
