        "v": 5,
        "title": "Web FAQ clarifies limited mode",
        "summary": "Added 'What is limited mode?' entry to home-client.tsx. Explains DeepSeek V4 Flash only and 5 one-hour sessions per day for VPN or non-full-access countries. Updated 'What models do you use?' and 'Which countries...' to distinguish full vs limited access. Minor documentation change.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:02:44.681Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The help page now clearly explains that people outside certain countries (or using a VPN) get a more restricted version of the service: they can only use one specific AI model, and only for up to 5 one-hour sessions per day. Visitors reading the FAQ will see a new section answering 'What is limited mode?', and the existing sections about which countries are supported and which models are offered have been adjusted to make the difference between full and limited access more obvious.",
